I can't reproduce, and the stacktrace is really strange: it points to a blank line inside the non-existent constructor of the ErrorActivity. I have no idea what it is about

> Note: Regarding "throws random errors every once in a while", for me it always errors out on every request. Then it always works on a retry. Is that how you intend it to work?

@opusforlife2 the errors are not completely random, but happen based on the value of a counter. In particular, chosen `x` and `y` for a type of exception, the exception will be thrown `if ((counter + x) % y == 0)`. So every time the app is opened the behaviour will be the same, since the counter resets to `0` and the outcomes are deterministic. But if you navigate in the app a little bit this should change.
